sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, Recall analytics-plausible-via-swamp (disable keeps the Plausible site), DECISIONS, R1-R4. docs/reference/analytics.md.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 3, 8, 17, 22 (DNS first and only outside the TLD; sites and certificates withdrawn in one step, as route:destroy does).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:analytics:disable
  %% kind: analytics.disable
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>serves the host
  CLI->>GW: instance:analytics:disable<br/>42
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:analytics:disable 42`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> [--yes] [--json]`
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - without `--yes`, the CLI asks first; the default is No
  %%> - without a terminal, or with `--json`, `--yes` is required (`input.confirmation_required`)
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes every tracking host of Instance 42; Plausible keeps the site and its history
  Note over CLI: Confirm host removal
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - asks for default-No consent before sending the disable request
  opt --yes
    Note over CLI: Skip the removal prompt
    %%> What it changes:
    %%> - supplies consent without the default-No prompt; required for noninteractive or JSON calls
  end
  Note over GW: Validate, find the hosts<br/>Instance lock
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - no other analytics or Route change runs for Instance 42; the Gateway holds one lock
  %%> Decides:
  %%> - whether any tracking host exists
  alt Instance has no hosts
    Note over GW: Nothing to remove<br/>R1: no run
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing changes; no Swamp run starts (R1)
    GW-->>CLI: Analytics disabled<br/>no hosts
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the final result at once; there is nothing to follow
  else hosts exist
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-analytics-disable
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - records task #5127 and starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the tracking sites and certificates to remove, and their DNS records
    %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - Plausible credentials; disable does not call Plausible
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5127
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task number, at once
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
    opt host outside the TLD
      Note over SW: Remove private DNS<br/>Node 1 over @swamp/ssh
      %%> When:
      %%> - only for a tracking host outside the Cluster or Node TLD; private DNS answers the whole TLD
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - removes the hosts' private DNS records and waits the 31-second grace
      %%> How:
      %%> - over SSH from 209 to the VPN Node (Node 1), with the `swamp` role's key
      %%> Why first:
      %%> - unpublish before removing: the name stops resolving before its site leaves
    end
    SW->>N: Withdraw sites, certs<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file absent
    %%> How:
    %%> - over SSH from 209 with `@swamp/ssh` and `@swamp/cfgmgmt/file`; `caddy validate` as one `@swamp/ssh exec`, then a reload
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes only the tracking sections; other sites stay; validates, then reloads Caddy without a restart
    %%> - on a Router, then removes the tracking certificates in the same step; tracking hosts on a Node-scoped Route have no Orbit certificate
    %%> Why one step:
    %%> - the mirror of `instance:analytics:enable`, and of `route:destroy`; the site goes before its certificate, so no read of the loaded config runs first
    SW->>N: Check the hosts are gone<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file check
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the loaded Caddy config and checks no tracking site remains
    alt every step passes
      N-->>SW: no tracking sites
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the check passed
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Delete tracking Routes<br/>binding gone · task succeeded
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the tracking Routes and the site binding are deleted
      %%> - the Plausible site, its history and its goals stay
      %%> - task #5127 succeeds
    else a step fails
      N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or site remains
      %%> When:
      %%> - Caddy refuses the config, SSH fails, or a tracking site is still loaded
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      %%> The Gateway reads:
      %%> - which step failed and its error code
      Note over GW: Keep Routes, mark failed<br/>task failed · rerun after a fix
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the tracking Routes and the site binding stay, marked failed; task #5127 fails
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - sections already withdrawn stay withdrawn; there is no rollback
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the same command again; it skips what is already gone
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show #5127
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
    end
  end
